      "html": "<div class=\"ds-sizes\"><span class=\"ds-size ds-small\">2.9 MB</span><span class=\"ds-size ds-medium\">10.0 MB</span><span class=\"ds-size ds-large\">40.1 MB</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-sizes{display:flex;gap:7px;}.ds-size{display:inline-block;padding:3px 6px;border-radius:4px;font-size:10px;font-weight:500;white-space:nowrap;}.ds-small{background:#edfaef;color:#185b2a;}.ds-medium{background:#fcf3cf;color:#694c00;}.ds-large{background:#fce8e8;color:#8a2424;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Selection summary",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "summary-card",
      "description": "Counts and measured-size context beside the comparison workspace.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-summary\"><h2>Ready to pull</h2><p>8 tables \u00b7 1 plugin \u00b7 0 themes \u00b7 no media files</p><dl><div><dt>Database</dt><dd>8 tables<small>~61.2 MB</small></dd></div><div><dt>Plugins</dt><dd>1 folder</dd></div></dl><p>Files are verified before replacement. A backup is saved automatically.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-summary{background:#fff;color:#1e2939;border:1px solid #dce4ed;border-radius:11px;padding:23px 20px;width:270px;max-width:100%;}.ds-summary h2{margin:0;font-size:17px;line-height:1.5;}.ds-summary p{color:#647184;font-size:11px;line-height:1.7;}.ds-summary dl{margin:19px 0 0;}.ds-summary dl>div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;padding:13px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #edf1f6;font-size:11px;}.ds-summary dt{color:#647184;}.ds-summary dd{margin:0;text-align:right;font-weight:550;}.ds-summary small{display:block;margin-top:4px;font-size:10px;font-weight:400;color:#647184;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Component rail",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "component-rail",
      "description": "Current component and inclusion are separate controls.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-rail\"><div class=\"ds-rail-entry ds-current\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" checked>Database</label><small>8 of 8 selected</small><button aria-label=\"Inspect database\" aria-expanded=\"true\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.75\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"/></svg></button></div><div class=\"ds-rail-entry\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\">Plugins</label><small>None selected</small><button aria-label=\"Inspect plugins\" aria-expanded=\"false\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.75\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"/></svg></button></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-rail{width:171px;background:#f6f8fc;border:1px solid #dce4ed;border-radius:11px;overflow:clip;}.ds-rail-entry{position:relative;min-height:70px;padding:12px 10px 12px 14px;display:grid;align-content:center;gap:5px;}.ds-current{background:#e8f0fb;color:#165c94;}.ds-rail label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;font-size:12px;font-weight:550;}.ds-rail input{margin:0;accent-color:#2271b1;}.ds-rail small{margin-left:24px;color:#647184;font-size:10px;line-height:1.5;}.ds-rail button{position:absolute;right:5px;top:17px;width:25px;height:36px;border:0;background:transparent;color:#72829a;cursor:pointer;}.ds-rail button[aria-expanded=\"false\"] svg{transform:rotate(-90deg);}.ds-rail button:hover{background:#e9ecef;}.ds-rail :is(button,input):focus-visible{outline:2px solid #2271b1;outline-offset:3px;box-shadow:none;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Telemetry canvas",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "telemetry-card",
      "description": "Dark monitoring material with real units and distinct verification.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-telemetry\"><div class=\"ds-stats\"><div>Received<strong>17.6 MiB / 19.1 MiB</strong></div><div>Transfer speed<strong>0.1 MB/s</strong></div><div>Stream remaining<strong>~10s</strong></div></div><p>Snapshot progress</p><div class=\"ds-byte-range\" aria-label=\"Received and verified stream bytes\"><span class=\"ds-verified\"></span><span class=\"ds-received\"></span></div><div class=\"ds-legend\"><span>Received</span><span>Verified</span></div></section>",
      "css": ".ds-telemetry{background:#172b43;color:#edf5ff;border-radius:12px;padding:26px 28px 22px;}.ds-stats{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:18px 30px;color:#b7c8dc;font-size:10px;margin-bottom:22px;}.ds-stats>div{flex:1;min-width:100px;}.ds-stats strong{display:block;color:#f0f6ff;font-size:22px;font-weight:550;line-height:1.4;margin-top:9px;letter-spacing:-.02em;}.ds-telemetry p{color:#c3d2e4;font-size:11px;}.ds-byte-range{display:flex;height:84px;background:#263d57;}.ds-verified{width:75%;background:#a587c1;}.ds-received{width:17%;background:#315b82;border-right:1px solid #80bdff;}.ds-legend{display:flex;gap:18px;color:#b7c8dc;font-size:10px;padding-top:14px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Transfer pipeline",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "pipeline-card",
      "description": "Text states accompany pipeline tracks.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-pipeline\"><h3>Transfer pipeline</h3><div class=\"ds-pipeline-row\"><div><strong>Database</strong><small>14.3 MiB / 14.3 MiB</small></div><div class=\"ds-track\"><span></span></div><small>Verified</small></div><p>Database and files are verified as complete streams.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-pipeline{background:#fff;border:1px solid #dce4ed;border-radius:11px;padding:22px 20px 15px;}.ds-pipeline h3{margin:0 0 15px;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:#26384d;}.ds-pipeline-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(100px,1fr) minmax(50px,1fr) 90px;align-items:center;gap:14px;padding:15px 0;border-top:1px solid #e5ebf3;}.ds-pipeline strong{display:block;font-size:11px;font-weight:550;color:#30455f;}.ds-pipeline small{display:block;font-size:9px;margin-top:5px;color:#647184;}.ds-pipeline-row>small{text-align:right;}.ds-track{height:5px;border-radius:3px;overflow:hidden;background:#eaf0f6;}.ds-track span{display:block;width:100%;height:100%;border-radius:3px;background:#a587c1;}.ds-pipeline p{font-size:9px;color:#647184;margin-top:12px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Recent activity",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "recent-activity",
      "description": "Always-visible timestamped monitoring events.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-activity\"><h3>Recent activity</h3><ol><li><time>01:38:56 AM</time><span>Receiving file stream</span><code>plugins/contact-form-7</code></li><li><time>01:38:57 AM</time><span>Connection restored</span></li></ol></section>",
      "css": ".ds-activity h3{margin:0 0 15px;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:#26384d;}.ds-activity ol{max-height:360px;overflow:auto;margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none;}.ds-activity li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content minmax(0,1fr);gap:4px 12px;padding:13px 0;border-top:1px solid #e2e9f2;color:#1e2939;font-size:11px;}.ds-activity time{grid-row:span 2;font-size:10px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:#647184;}.ds-activity code{font-size:10px;background:none;padding:0;color:#56636c;overflow-wrap:anywhere;}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The transfer workbench",
    "overview": "Trickle gives administrators a compact, deliberate workspace for consequential transfers. Source and destination remain explicit, selection details sit beside comparison data, and primary actions retain WordPress blue. The interface uses short labels, quiet supporting text, thin dividers, and rounded white surfaces.\n\nMonitoring changes the working material to a dark navy telemetry canvas. Bright measurements and muted chart scaffolding make received, pending, and verified work distinguishable. Pipeline and recent activity explain the operation beneath the chart. This document records the implemented migration workspace and monitor; the shared settings, backups, and diagnostics components remain an incumbent system rather than a newly redesigned surface.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dense comparison data with a persistent wide-screen selection summary.",
      "White, bordered setup surfaces and a navy monitoring canvas.",
      "Measured progress, separate verification state, and readable activity history.",
      "WordPress blue actions and concise operational copy."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Verification Rule",
        "body": "Received work and verified work must remain visually distinct; lavender is reserved for confirmed stream verification.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** retain WordPress blue for primary transfer actions and visible keyboard focus.",
      "**Do** preserve source, destination, and selected-component context throughout the workflow.",
      "**Do** distinguish received bytes from verified streams using both color and text.",
      "**Do** show measured units and omit unsupported speed or ETA estimates.",
      "**Do** keep pipeline and recent activity visible in monitoring, stacking them on narrow screens.",
      "**Do** preserve the existing shared components when extending settings, backups, and diagnostics."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** apply the dark telemetry material to the entire setup workspace.",
      "**Don't** mark received bytes as verified before stream verification succeeds.",
      "**Don't** squeeze comparison tables into unreadable mobile columns; preserve horizontal scrolling.",
      "**Don't** promote the migration rail and summary arrangement into a requirement for unrelated plugin surfaces."
    ]
  }
}
